BOCA-CM
=======

BOCA-CM is BOCA (https://github.com/cassiopc/boca) with a code editor in the
team's Runs page, based on CodeMirror 5:

  * syntax highlighting for C, C++, Java, Kotlin and Python (chosen from the
    extension of the contest language);
  * several tabs, saved in the browser, so code survives the periodic page reload;
  * "Send" asks for the file name (with a suggestion) and submits the code through
    the same upload used by the original BOCA - the server side is unchanged;
  * "[edit]" next to a previous run opens its code in a new tab;
  * "Open file" loads a local file into the editor.

and with the number of passed tests of each run:

  * the autojudge counts passed tests ("[3/10]" at the start of the autojudge
    answer). After a wrong answer it keeps running the remaining tests to count
    them, but the verdict is still the one of the first failing test; a time
    limit or runtime error still stops the judging;
  * the admin sees the count in the "AJ" column of the Runs page;
  * options on the admin's Runs page: release autojudge answers to teams
    automatically, and show the number of passed tests to teams.

Installation is the same as for BOCA: CodeMirror is bundled in src/codemirror,
so there are no extra dependencies and no internet access is needed. There are
no database changes; an existing BOCA install can be updated by replacing the
files in /var/www/boca/src.

Step-by-step installation guide (clean install or on top of an existing BOCA),
in Portuguese: doc/INSTALL-BOCA-CM.md

Please find the BOCA documentation in the doc/ folder.
